# Eliminate Preview Lag with MediaBunny + Backend Optimization

## Problem Analysis

After reading the full codebase, here is your **exact lag architecture**:

### Current Flow (Why It's Slow)

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User as User (Browser)
    participant Client as client1 (Next.js)
    participant Backend as backend1 (Bun)
    participant FFmpeg as FFmpeg Process

    User->>Client: Scrubs timeline to 15s
    Client->>Backend: POST /api/project/:id/preview/segment {playheadTime: 15}
    Backend->>FFmpeg: Spawn ffmpeg process
    Note over FFmpeg: 1. Concatenate all audio WAVs
    Note over FFmpeg: 2. Seek template video to 15s
    Note over FFmpeg: 3. Build complex filter graph (overlays, characters, subtitles)
    Note over FFmpeg: 4. Encode 3s MP4 segment
    FFmpeg-->>Backend: seg_15000_3000.mp4 (2-8 seconds later)
    Backend-->>Client: {url: "/previews/segments/..."}
    Client->>Backend: GET segment MP4
    Backend-->>Client: MP4 bytes
    Client->>User: Video element loads & displays
    Note over User: Total lag: 3-10 seconds per scrub
```

### Root Cause

Every single scrub/playhead change triggers in [previewGenerator.ts:1496-2002](file:///f:/Aniruddha/code/webdev/PROJECTS/aislop/backend1/src/service/previewGenerator.ts#L1496-L2002):
1. **Audio concatenation** — re-concatenates ALL audio WAVs every time
2. **FFmpeg process spawn** — full process start overhead
3. **Complex filter graph** — overlays, characters, subtitles ASS generation
4. **Video encoding** — encodes a 3s MP4 even at 360x640

For **Play**, [previewGenerator.ts:1120-1482](file:///f:/Aniruddha/code/webdev/PROJECTS/aislop/backend1/src/service/previewGenerator.ts#L1120-L1482) generates a full HLS playlist with *all* overlays composited — taking 15-60s before the user sees anything.

### Proposed Flow (Instant)

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User as User (Browser)
    participant Engine as MediaBunny Engine (Browser)
    participant Canvas as Canvas Compositor (Browser)
    participant Backend as backend1 (Bun)

    Note over User,Backend: ONE-TIME: Backend sends manifest + asset URLs on project load
    Backend-->>Engine: Template video URL + Audio URLs + Overlay image URLs

    User->>Engine: Scrubs timeline to 15s
    Engine->>Engine: videoSink.getSample(15) → VideoFrame (GPU-decoded, <5ms)
    Engine->>Canvas: Draw template frame
    Canvas->>Canvas: Draw overlay images at correct positions (from timeline data)
    Canvas->>Canvas: Draw character sprites
    Canvas->>Canvas: Draw karaoke subtitles (CSS/Canvas text)
    Canvas->>User: Composited frame displayed instantly
    Note over User: Total lag: <16ms (one frame)
```

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **This plan adds MediaBunny as a client-side dependency (~50KB gzipped).** Your backend FFmpeg pipeline is preserved exactly as-is for the **final export** — MediaBunny only replaces the **preview layer** in the browser.

> [!WARNING]
> **WebCodecs browser support:** Chrome 94+, Edge 94+, Safari 16.4+, Firefox 130+. If you need to support older browsers, the plan includes a fallback to your current segment-based approach.

## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> 1. **Template videos:** Your templates are stored on the backend filesystem. Do users typically use the same 2-3 templates, or are they uploading new ones frequently? This affects whether we pre-convert them to browser-friendly formats.
> 2. **Overlay images:** Are your overlay images always PNG/JPEG, or do you also have video overlays (Hyperframes animations) that need to play inline? The plan handles both, but video overlays add complexity.
> 3. **Audio preview:** Do you want audio to play during scrubbing (scrub audio), or is visual-only scrub feedback sufficient? Full audio scrub requires Web Audio API integration.

---

## Proposed Changes

### Phase 1: Client-Side Canvas Compositor (Instant Scrub Preview)

Replace the server-round-trip segment preview with a client-side canvas that composites template frame + overlays + characters + subtitles directly in the browser.

---

#### [NEW] [mediaEngine.ts](file:///f:/Aniruddha/code/webdev/PROJECTS/aislop/client1/src/lib/mediaEngine.ts)

Core MediaBunny wrapper for GPU-accelerated frame extraction.

```typescript
// client1/src/lib/mediaEngine.ts
import {
  Input,
  ALL_FORMATS,
  UrlSource,
  VideoSampleSink,
} from 'mediabunny';

export class MediaEngine {
  private input: Input | null = null;
  private videoSink: VideoSampleSink | null = null;
  private ready = false;

  /** Load a template video from a URL (served by backend) */
  async load(videoUrl: string): Promise<void> {
    this.dispose();
    this.input = new Input({
      formats: ALL_FORMATS,
      source: new UrlSource(videoUrl),
    });
    const videoTrack = await this.input.getPrimaryVideoTrack();
    if (!videoTrack || !(await videoTrack.canDecode())) {
      throw new Error('Video track not decodable via WebCodecs');
    }
    this.videoSink = new VideoSampleSink(videoTrack);
    this.ready = true;
  }

  /** Get a decoded VideoFrame at a specific timestamp (GPU-accelerated) */
  async getFrameAtTime(
    timeSeconds: number,
    ctx: CanvasRenderingContext2D,
    width: number,
    height: number
  ): Promise<void> {
    if (!this.videoSink || !this.ready) return;
    const sample = await this.videoSink.getSample(timeSeconds);
    if (sample) {
      sample.draw(ctx, 0, 0, width, height);
      sample.close();
    }
  }

  /** Check if WebCodecs is available in this browser */
  static isSupported(): boolean {
    return typeof VideoDecoder !== 'undefined'
      && typeof VideoEncoder !== 'undefined';
  }

  dispose(): void {
    this.videoSink = null;
    this.input = null;
    this.ready = false;
  }
}
```

---

#### [NEW] [canvasCompositor.ts](file:///f:/Aniruddha/code/webdev/PROJECTS/aislop/client1/src/lib/canvasCompositor.ts)

Client-side compositor that draws template frame + overlays + characters + subtitles onto a single `<canvas>`.

```typescript
// client1/src/lib/canvasCompositor.ts
import type { EditorProject, Clip, OverlayClip, CharacterClip, SubtitleClip } from '@/features/editor/types';
import { MediaEngine } from './mediaEngine';
import { API_ENDPOINTS } from '@/config/api';

type CachedImage = { img: HTMLImageElement; loaded: boolean };

export class CanvasCompositor {
  private canvas: HTMLCanvasElement;
  private ctx: CanvasRenderingContext2D;
  private engine: MediaEngine;
  private imageCache = new Map<string, CachedImage>();
  private width = 360;
  private height = 640;

  constructor(canvas: HTMLCanvasElement) {
    this.canvas = canvas;
    this.canvas.width = this.width;
    this.canvas.height = this.height;
    this.ctx = canvas.getContext('2d')!;
    this.engine = new MediaEngine();
  }

  async loadTemplate(videoUrl: string): Promise<void> {
    await this.engine.load(videoUrl);
  }

  /** Preload overlay and character images into cache */
  preloadImages(project: EditorProject): void {
    for (const track of project.tracks) {
      for (const clip of track.clips) {
        if (clip.kind === 'overlay') {
          const oc = clip as OverlayClip;
          const url = API_ENDPOINTS.serveProjectImage(project.id, oc.assetId);
          this.cacheImage(oc.assetId, url);
        }
        if (clip.kind === 'character') {
          const cc = clip as CharacterClip;
          const key = `char_${cc.character}_${cc.emotion || 'default'}`;
          // Character images served from backend static path
          const url = `/api/video/character/${cc.character}/${cc.emotion || 'default'}`;
          this.cacheImage(key, url);
        }
      }
    }
  }

  private cacheImage(key: string, url: string): void {
    if (this.imageCache.has(key)) return;
    const img = new Image();
    img.crossOrigin = 'anonymous';
    const entry: CachedImage = { img, loaded: false };
    img.onload = () => { entry.loaded = true; };
    img.src = url;
    this.imageCache.set(key, entry);
  }

  /** Render a single composited frame at the given timeline time */
  async renderFrame(project: EditorProject, timeSeconds: number): Promise<void> {
    const ctx = this.ctx;
    const w = this.width;
    const h = this.height;

    // 1. Clear canvas
    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, w, h);

    // 2. Draw template video frame (GPU-decoded via MediaBunny)
    await this.engine.getFrameAtTime(timeSeconds, ctx, w, h);

    // 3. Draw overlays active at this time
    this.drawOverlays(project, timeSeconds, ctx, w, h);

    // 4. Draw characters active at this time
    this.drawCharacters(project, timeSeconds, ctx, w, h);

    // 5. Draw subtitle text active at this time
    this.drawSubtitles(project, timeSeconds, ctx, w, h);
  }

  private drawOverlays(
    project: EditorProject, t: number,
    ctx: CanvasRenderingContext2D, w: number, h: number
  ): void {
    for (const track of project.tracks) {
      if (track.type !== 'overlay') continue;
      for (const clip of track.clips) {
        const oc = clip as OverlayClip;
        if (t < oc.start || t > oc.start + oc.duration) continue;
        if (oc.planStatus === 'draft') continue;

        const cached = this.imageCache.get(oc.assetId);
        if (!cached?.loaded) continue;

        if (oc.displayMode === 'replace') {
          // Full-frame replacement
          ctx.drawImage(cached.img, 0, 0, w, h);
        } else {
          // Positioned overlay
          const scale = oc.scale || 0.5;
          const ow = Math.floor(w * scale);
          const oh = Math.floor(h * scale * 0.75);
          const ox = Math.floor(oc.x * w - ow / 2);
          const oy = Math.floor(oc.y * h - oh / 2);
          ctx.drawImage(cached.img, ox, oy, ow, oh);
        }
      }
    }
  }

  private drawCharacters(
    project: EditorProject, t: number,
    ctx: CanvasRenderingContext2D, w: number, h: number
  ): void {
    const SCALE = h / 1920;
    const charGeom: Record<string, { x: number; y: number; w: number; h: number }> = {
      Stewie: { x: Math.floor(300 * SCALE), y: Math.floor(1350 * SCALE), w: Math.floor(500 * SCALE), h: Math.floor(600 * SCALE) },
      Peter:  { x: Math.floor(300 * SCALE), y: Math.floor(1250 * SCALE), w: Math.floor(580 * SCALE), h: Math.floor(720 * SCALE) },
    };
    const defaultGeom = { x: Math.floor(260 * SCALE), y: Math.floor(1160 * SCALE), w: Math.floor(560 * SCALE), h: Math.floor(760 * SCALE) };

    for (const track of project.tracks) {
      if (track.type !== 'character') continue;
      for (const clip of track.clips) {
        const cc = clip as CharacterClip;
        if (t < cc.start || t > cc.start + cc.duration) continue;

        const key = `char_${cc.character}_${cc.emotion || 'default'}`;
        const cached = this.imageCache.get(key);
        if (!cached?.loaded) continue;

        const geom = charGeom[cc.character] || defaultGeom;
        ctx.drawImage(cached.img, geom.x, geom.y, geom.w, geom.h);
      }
    }
  }

  private drawSubtitles(
    project: EditorProject, t: number,
    ctx: CanvasRenderingContext2D, w: number, h: number
  ): void {
    const SCALE = h / 1920;
    const fontSize = Math.floor(48 * SCALE);
    const marginV = Math.floor(700 * SCALE);
    const baseY = h - marginV;

    for (const track of project.tracks) {
      if (track.type !== 'subtitle') continue;
      for (const clip of track.clips) {
        const sc = clip as SubtitleClip;
        if (t < sc.start || t > sc.start + sc.duration) continue;

        // Find active word for karaoke highlight
        const relTime = t - sc.start;
        const words = sc.words || [];
        let activeWordIdx = -1;
        for (let i = 0; i < words.length; i++) {
          if (relTime >= words[i].start && relTime < words[i].end) {
            activeWordIdx = i;
            break;
          }
        }

        // Draw 3-word groups with karaoke highlighting
        ctx.textAlign = 'center';
        ctx.textBaseline = 'middle';

        if (words.length > 0) {
          // Find which 3-word group the active word belongs to
          const groupStart = Math.floor((activeWordIdx >= 0 ? activeWordIdx : 0) / 3) * 3;
          const groupWords = words.slice(groupStart, groupStart + 3);

          let xOffset = w / 2;
          const totalText = groupWords.map(w => w.word).join(' ');

          // Draw shadow
          ctx.font = `bold ${fontSize}px Arial-Black, Arial, sans-serif`;
          ctx.strokeStyle = 'black';
          ctx.lineWidth = fontSize * 0.15;
          ctx.strokeText(totalText, xOffset, baseY);

          // Draw each word with color
          let charX = xOffset - ctx.measureText(totalText).width / 2;
          for (let i = 0; i < groupWords.length; i++) {
            const wordText = groupWords[i].word + (i < groupWords.length - 1 ? ' ' : '');
            const isActive = (groupStart + i) === activeWordIdx;
            ctx.fillStyle = isActive ? '#FFFF00' : '#FFFFFF';
            ctx.textAlign = 'left';
            ctx.fillText(wordText, charX, baseY);
            charX += ctx.measureText(wordText).width;
          }
        } else {
          // Fallback: render plain text
          ctx.font = `bold ${fontSize}px Arial-Black, Arial, sans-serif`;
          ctx.fillStyle = '#FFFFFF';
          ctx.strokeStyle = 'black';
          ctx.lineWidth = fontSize * 0.15;
          ctx.strokeText(sc.text, w / 2, baseY);
          ctx.fillText(sc.text, w / 2, baseY);
        }
        break; // Only render first active subtitle
      }
    }
  }

  dispose(): void {
    this.engine.dispose();
    this.imageCache.clear();
  }
}
```

