### Phase 2: Backend Optimization (Faster HLS/Export)

Even with client-side scrub, you still need HLS for full playback and FFmpeg for final export. These changes make both significantly faster.

---

#### [MODIFY] [previewGenerator.ts](file:///f:/Aniruddha/code/webdev/PROJECTS/aislop/backend1/src/service/previewGenerator.ts)

**Optimization 1: Cache concatenated audio.** Lines 803-821 re-concatenate ALL audio WAVs on every preview request. This is ~2-5 seconds of wasted time.

```diff
 // Line ~803: Add audio cache
+const audioCache = new Map<string, { path: string; timestamp: number }>();
+
+function getCachedAudioPath(projectId: string, audioSessionId: string): string | null {
+  const key = `${projectId}_${audioSessionId}`;
+  const cached = audioCache.get(key);
+  if (cached && fs.existsSync(cached.path)) return cached.path;
+  return null;
+}

 // In generateTimelinePreviewHls, replace audio concat block:
+const cachedAudio = getCachedAudioPath(projectId, audioSessionId);
+let concatenatedAudioPath: string;
+let audioListPath: string | null = null;
+
+if (cachedAudio) {
+  concatenatedAudioPath = cachedAudio;
+} else {
   // ... existing concat logic ...
+  audioCache.set(`${projectId}_${audioSessionId}`, {
+    path: concatenatedAudioPath,
+    timestamp: Date.now(),
+  });
+}
```

**Optimization 2: Skip segment preview entirely when WebCodecs is active.** Add a query param so the client can signal it doesn't need segment previews.

```diff
 // In the segment preview route handler (projectController.ts):
+// If client signals WebCodecs support, return immediately
+if (ctx.query?.clientDecoder === 'webcodecs') {
+  return { status: 200, body: { success: true, state: 'skipped', reason: 'client_webcodecs' } };
+}
