## Summary of Changes

| Layer | File | Change | Impact |
|-------|------|--------|--------|
| **client1** | `src/lib/mediaEngine.ts` | [NEW] MediaBunny wrapper for GPU frame extraction | Instant frame decode |
| **client1** | `src/lib/canvasCompositor.ts` | [NEW] Canvas-based compositor for overlays+chars+subs | Zero-latency compositing |
| **client1** | `src/lib/audioEngine.ts` | [NEW] Web Audio API for scrub audio (optional) | Audio during scrub |
| **client1** | `components/editor/CanvasPreview.tsx` | [MODIFY] Add canvas layer, use compositor on scrub | **Eliminates segment round-trips** |
| **client1** | `components/editor/EditorLayout.tsx` | [MODIFY] Skip segment requests when WebCodecs available | Reduces backend load |
| **client1** | `package.json` | [MODIFY] Add `mediabunny` dependency | ~50KB gzipped |
| **backend1** | `service/previewGenerator.ts` | [MODIFY] Cache concatenated audio | 2-5s faster HLS/segment |
| **backend1** | `router.ts` or routes | [NEW] Character image serve endpoint | Client compositor needs images |

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
1. `npm run build` in both `client1` and `backend1` — no type errors
2. Open editor in Chrome DevTools → Performance tab → scrub the timeline
   - **Before:** Network waterfall shows segment POST requests on each scrub
   - **After:** Zero network requests during scrub; canvas repaints in <16ms
3. Console log `[PreviewTelemetry]` events to measure `play_click_to_first_frame_ms`

### Manual Verification
1. Open editor → scrub timeline rapidly → preview updates instantly (no "Generating preview..." overlay)
2. Press Play → HLS playback works exactly as before (with all overlays composited by backend)
3. Press Export → Final export works exactly as before (backend FFmpeg pipeline untouched)
4. Open in Firefox/Safari → Falls back to existing segment-based preview gracefully
5. Load a project with overlay images + character sprites + karaoke subtitles → all render correctly on the canvas compositor during scrub
